# src/common

Cross-pack helpers (`deterministic-reader`, `generate-context`, `generate-entry`, `fill`, `compile-filter`) live in `@deterministic-code/generators-common`. Import them from that package. Do not re-export them from this repo.

Keep pack-specific modules here: `type-converter.ts`. YAML parsing (`DeterministicParser`, specification types) lives in `@deterministic-code/deterministic-specifications-typescript/parser`. Filename constants (`TYPES_YAML`, `ROUTES_YAML`, …) and helpers (`typeHasTag`, `primaryKeyColumn`) live in `@deterministic-code/generators-common/spec-types`. File layout and crate specifiers live in pack `src/import-generator.ts` (`RustImportGenerator` / `createImportGenerator`). `IImportGenerator` is imported from generators-common. `other.organize_by_feature` is read only in that class constructor — never in generate-*.ts or `PackCasing`. Generators must not compose prefixes, `features/`, or `crate::` paths; they only call ImportGenerator methods. Do not copy generators-common sources back into this repo. Do not put new files under `src/sdk/`.

`generate` is the only export each lane has. It takes `GenerateContext`: `{ reader, settings }` where `reader` is `{ read, exists }` (`IDeterministicReader`) and `settings` is the flat string dict (`application_name`, …). The host never supplies pack-normalized types — each lane's exported `generate` reads YAML and parses once via `DeterministicParser`. Emit logic lives in an internal `generateFrom(deterministic, settings)` that reads `IDeterministic` (`types`, `expandedTypes`, `datasource`, `services`, `routes`, `datasourceSeeds`) and treats `expandedTypes` (via `datasourceTypesOf` / `viewTypesOf`) as the final field lists. Map those fields as-is — do not strip inherited `set` columns or rebuild lists with `tableFields` or `parentFields`. Authored `types` are for metadata (kind, inherits, omit via `removeFields`) only. Do not add per-lane aliases (`generateBackendApp`, `generateDatasourceTypes`, …) or host flags (`pinProjectRoot`, `rustModuleWiring`, `assembleAfterStep`). Import `GenerateEntry` from `@deterministic-code/generators-common/generate-entry`, not from a lane module.
